An array contains distinct numbers from 0 through n, with exactly one number missing. Find the missing number.
Example: nums = [3, 0, 1]
Output: 2
Explanation: The complete sequence is 0, 1, 2, 3.


Solution:

const nums = [3, 0, 1];
const set = new Set(nums);
lenth = nums.length + 1;
let missingNumber = 0;

for (let i = 0; i < lenth; i++) {
  if (!set.has(i)) {
    missingNumber = i;
  }
}

console.log(missingNumber);
